    "stem": "Show that $k = 2$.",
    "answerSpec": {
     "markScheme": {
      "points": [
       {
        "id": "p1",
        "description": "M1 uses $(k + 4)^2 = k(k + 16)$.",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p2",
        "description": "A1 expands to $k^2 + 8k + 16 = k^2 + 16k$, so $8k = 16$ and $k = 2$.",
        "marks": 1
       }
      ]
     },
     "modelAnswer": "$$\n\\frac{k + 4}{k} = \\frac{k + 16}{k + 4} \\Rightarrow (k + 4)^2 = k(k + 16)\n$$\n\n$$\nk^2 + 8k + 16 = k^2 + 16k \\Rightarrow 8k = 16 \\Rightarrow k = 2\n$$"
    },
    "explanation": "Equal ratios of consecutive terms."
   },
